WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.210 --> 00:00:03.800
- And sometimes when I
be telling these stories

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:08.187
I be crying, but I be
crying from the inside.

00:00:08.187 --> 00:00:09.820
You never see a teardrop,

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:12.423
but on the inside, I've
been crying all my life.

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:15.310
I've been crying of all my life.

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:17.690
But God's been crying with me.

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:19.140
I've been crying all my life.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:24.790
- [Mark] All right, David.

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:26.880
David, where'd you grow
up, where are you from?

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:30.433
- I'm originally from San Francisco.

00:00:33.631 --> 00:00:38.070
And as I was growing up,
still as the teenager,

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:41.513
a little boy, my mom moved to Pasadena.

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:48.550
But as a kid, I was raised in Pasadena

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:50.620
but I didn't know nothing but Pasadena.

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:54.840
I didn't know if I go too
far where I am, I'm lost.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:58.300
So I caught a bus one day and this bus

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:01.790
landed me at skid row
on fifth and Broadway.

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:04.690
And it was alive, in 1975.

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:09.690
It was alive, bars open 24 hours a day.

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:12.810
People walking back and forth.

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:13.970
Just a whole bunch of traffic

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:16.533
a whole bunch of activity going on.

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:20.340
- [Mark] What age were you?

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:21.773
- Oh, 17.

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:27.670
Yes. And I lived here in skid row from 17

00:01:28.127 --> 00:01:33.127
and may the 12th, I'll be 62 years old.

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:34.940
And I'm still here.

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:38.220
You see 48 years later.

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:41.950
Once I left Pasadena, I
never went back to my family.

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:43.170
I've been out here ever since.

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:45.713
So everybody didn't know where I was.

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:49.210
- [Mark] How was your childhood?

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:52.960
- Oh, my childhood, I
remember a lot of things that

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:54.763
haunted me all my life.

00:01:55.640 --> 00:02:00.430
Which is my uncle, one
day was babysitting me

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:03.040
for my mom, cause she was at work.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:05.160
And he had filled up the bathtub

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:10.160
with water and soap,
bath water, bath soap.

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:14.320
And he was naked and he
had me in there naked

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:17.440
and he had me sitting on top of him.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:22.300
And my mom she told me she
almost blew his brains out.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.760
Her own brother, when she walked in

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:29.663
and seen him have me naked on his lap.

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:34.095
And she pulled out a gun and she told me.

00:02:34.095 --> 00:02:38.380
She hated me ever since what she seen,

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:39.550
she hated me ever since.

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:40.383
- [Mark] She hated you?

00:02:40.383 --> 00:02:41.810
- She hated me.

00:02:41.810 --> 00:02:44.350
And for what happened to me.

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:49.110
Cause she never, ever got
to know who I really was

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:50.673
because I was afraid.

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:54.300
So I hid many personalities from my mom.

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:57.220
And at the age of six, she was drunk.

00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:58.960
And she said, you know what?

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:00.330
I hate you.

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:04.347
I hate you with a passion, you son a bitch

00:03:05.228 --> 00:03:07.559
and all this and thing, she cursed me.

00:03:07.559 --> 00:03:09.880
I asked her why I would shake the door,

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:11.630
I said, why you hate me, mom?

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:13.660
She said, because of your father.

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:17.060
I hated that motherfucker
for all that he done to me,

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:20.470
beat me in my stomach
so I couldn't have you.

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:22.670
And all of this stuff.

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:27.410
And ever since childhood I've been alone.

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:29.600
I've been here 48 years now.

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:30.750
- [Mark] Your dad?

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:32.290
- I never seen him.

00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:33.830
- [Mark] He hit your mom in the stomach?

00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:35.820
- Yeah, so she can have a miscarriage.

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:37.237
- [Mark] When she was carrying you?

00:03:37.237 --> 00:03:39.904
- Yes, she was pregnant with me.

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:43.570
What happened when he
hit her in her stomach,

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:45.490
it turned me around.

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:48.930
So when she was giving
birth, one of my legs

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:53.060
was stuck inside they were
me out backwards by my leg.

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:54.650
And this leg was inside.

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:57.960
So they didn't want me to drown, in my mom

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:02.200
they had to cut my
mom's vagina wide enough

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:04.630
to take my foot and leg out.

00:04:04.630 --> 00:04:08.250
So ever since then, my mom always said,

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:10.520
you know, you've been a hell of a problem

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:14.610
to me ever since you was born.

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:19.610
So in other words, she had to
cut it open and get me out.

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:22.750
My father beat her in her stomach

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:26.751
So, and you know, so she
hated him, so she hated me.

00:04:26.751 --> 00:04:27.670
Because she'd say you know what?

00:04:27.670 --> 00:04:30.730
You look just like him, you like his twin

00:04:30.730 --> 00:04:33.520
and you talk like him, and
I hate that motherfucker

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:36.960
so I hate you too, and
I was six years old.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:38.740
And these things,

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:43.053
see now I'm a diagnosed
paranoid schizophrenic,

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:49.380
bipolar and all kinds of
things cause of my lifestyle

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:52.373
in downtown here for 48 years,

00:04:53.397 --> 00:04:56.260
it did a hell of a toll on me.

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:59.720
But it didn't never make me weak.

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:01.520
It made me stronger.

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:05.220
Cause for 48 years, it
takes a hell of a person

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:09.350
to survive down in an area
like this for 48 years.

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:10.320
- [Mark] Are you living on the street?

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:14.180
- Yes, and underneath
the freeway, in the park

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:17.020
in alleys, in abandoned buildings,

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:19.603
wherever, abandoned car, wherever I can.

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:22.880
- [Mark] Are drugs a part of your life?

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:23.883
- Yes, they is.

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:29.579
When I came down here, I had
never used drugs in my life.

00:05:29.579 --> 00:05:30.412
So not even marijuana.

00:05:30.412 --> 00:05:33.400
So when I got to down
here, I met some people

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:34.720
and we made friends.

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:37.200
They taught me how to smoke marijuana.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:38.970
Then they told me how it taught me

00:05:38.970 --> 00:05:41.033
how to smoke crack cocaine.

00:05:44.883 --> 00:05:45.770
And spice.

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:48.576
Somebody had to show me
how to do these things.

00:05:48.576 --> 00:05:49.925
Because I never knew it.

00:05:49.925 --> 00:05:50.758
- [Mark] And what is your drug today?

00:05:50.758 --> 00:05:51.870
- My drug is spice.

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:54.090
- [Mark] Spice? What
does spice do for you?

00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:59.090
- Spice, for me it slows my thinking down.

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:04.950
It slows my thinking down to a point where

00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:09.950
I can understand whatever
my mind is trying to

00:06:10.690 --> 00:06:14.170
make me understand, I can figure it out.

00:06:14.170 --> 00:06:17.540
And this is what I been
doing for 48 years.

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:19.093
I've been figuring people out.

00:06:20.261 --> 00:06:21.770
Because there's so many
different personalities

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:25.910
so many different tragedies
happen in front of my eyes.

00:06:25.910 --> 00:06:29.050
I was standing closer from me to you,

00:06:29.050 --> 00:06:32.840
And this dude pull out a 357 Magnum,

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:36.230
put it to a dude's head, pow,

00:06:36.230 --> 00:06:38.490
blew his whole top of his head off

00:06:38.490 --> 00:06:42.900
his brain fragmented, splattered
all over the sidewalk.

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:45.920
They were still flapping
because of the nerves.

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:49.433
Blood and water came out,
whew, of the top of his head.

00:06:51.678 --> 00:06:54.333
And this thing made me suffer PTSD.

00:06:56.110 --> 00:06:57.700
You know, now I suffered.

00:06:57.700 --> 00:07:01.760
I take a lot of medication
and in my apartment now

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:04.420
I thank God, I'm not living
on the street no more.

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:08.458
For three years, God has blessed
me with a brand apartment.

00:07:08.458 --> 00:07:09.792
So I got a brand new apartment now.

00:07:09.792 --> 00:07:10.625
- [Mark] You got housing now?

00:07:10.625 --> 00:07:12.000
- Yeah.
- How long has that then?

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:13.340
- Three years.
- Three years?

00:07:13.340 --> 00:07:14.936
- Yeah.
- Good for you.

00:07:14.936 --> 00:07:18.160
- Cause I get my rent paid automatically,

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:21.610
I don't have to worry about
not having money to pay rent.

00:07:21.610 --> 00:07:23.610
They paid my rent for me.

00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:25.450
I'm under money management.

00:07:25.450 --> 00:07:29.230
So they issue me certain allowances out,

00:07:29.230 --> 00:07:32.020
but they keep my money for me.

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:33.930
That's nice, and it's
been over three years

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:36.150
they've been doing it for me.

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:37.919
- [Mark] Do you have children?

00:07:37.919 --> 00:07:39.036
- Never, no.

00:07:39.036 --> 00:07:39.869
- You ever been married?
- No.

00:07:39.869 --> 00:07:41.883
- You ever been in love?
- No.

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:45.523
- You feel like you were
ever loved as a child?

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:48.610
So you've never--
- So I've never

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:51.463
knew how love is supposed to feel.

00:07:52.540 --> 00:07:55.400
So when somebody told me, one girl told me

00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:59.810
I have never had no
sex since 48 years now,

00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:03.670
with a female, never
have sex for 48 years.

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:07.690
Why? Because I met one girl when I was 17

00:08:08.539 --> 00:08:11.100
and I was in YA,
California Youth Authority.

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:12.420
They took me to the hospital.

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:15.210
She was a secretary, so we got to meet.

00:08:15.210 --> 00:08:16.940
And she said, oh, David,

00:08:16.940 --> 00:08:18.930
after three days we know each other,

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:22.880
I love you, you're the
only man in my life.

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:25.760
And she led me to believe it.

00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:28.750
So I gave all my heart to her.

00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:32.370
Cause not knowing any better,
I gave my heart to her.

00:08:32.370 --> 00:08:34.933
Then later on down the
relationship, she said,

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:38.510
well I can't see you anymore.

00:08:38.510 --> 00:08:40.430
I say what you talking about?

00:08:40.430 --> 00:08:42.370
I thought you said you love me.

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:45.350
No, I'm in love, I'm married.

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:48.450
And she showed me a picture
of her, her husband and baby.

00:08:48.450 --> 00:08:50.723
I said, you know, it broke my,

00:08:50.723 --> 00:08:51.600
it did something mentally to me.

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:52.490
- [Mark] She was married.

00:08:52.490 --> 00:08:55.350
- Yeah. It did something mentally to me,

00:08:55.350 --> 00:08:58.471
just as well as broke my heart.

00:08:58.471 --> 00:09:03.400
So I never trusted women
since 48 years now.

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:05.422
I don't feel like I'm gay or anything.

00:09:05.422 --> 00:09:06.720
I don't have no feeling.

00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:08.853
It's numb, I don't know how to feel.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:12.220
You know, everything I went through

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:16.210
I had to feel now I don't want to feel

00:09:17.130 --> 00:09:18.030
- [Mark] Would you,
would you call yourself,

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:19.723
would you consider yourself happy?

00:09:22.520 --> 00:09:24.393
- Yeah. Yeah, in a way.

00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:28.290
Just because of the fact that I know

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:30.710
I'm in contact with God above

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:34.310
and he's been protecting
me ever since 48 years.

00:09:34.310 --> 00:09:36.370
- Does that help you?
- Yes, yes.

00:09:36.370 --> 00:09:40.563
My belief helps me
overcome a lot of things.

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:44.670
I believe that God is
gonna make a way for me

00:09:44.670 --> 00:09:46.690
to make everything alright.

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:49.620
So I just go through the motions,

00:09:49.620 --> 00:09:51.670
go through an episode but I know

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:53.280
I'm not going through it alone,

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:54.740
He's going through it with me

00:09:56.059 --> 00:09:57.073
and that make me happy.

00:09:58.050 --> 00:10:00.513
So I consider myself blessed.

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:04.820
- [Mark] Is this the best
time of your life right now?

00:10:04.820 --> 00:10:07.173
- Yes, as I grow old.

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:10.580
As I grow old, yes this is the best time.

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:12.435
When I look in the mirror now,

00:10:12.435 --> 00:10:14.270
see these gray hairs in my hair.

00:10:14.270 --> 00:10:18.369
I say, damn, David, I remember
when you had all black hair.

00:10:18.369 --> 00:10:20.616
And I be talking to myself
while I look in the mirror,

00:10:20.616 --> 00:10:25.230
It takes whether or not to
have that shit up there anyway.

00:10:25.230 --> 00:10:26.270
All the shit I been through,

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:28.327
it turned my hair gray anyway (laughs).

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:31.050
- [Mark] How old are you now?

00:10:31.050 --> 00:10:33.163
- 62, I'll be 63 in May.

00:10:36.180 --> 00:10:37.300
- [Mark] What's the most important lesson

00:10:37.300 --> 00:10:38.700
you've learned in your life?

00:10:39.960 --> 00:10:42.833
- Well, the most important, not to judge.

00:10:44.050 --> 00:10:46.050
Not to judge no one.
- That's a good one.

00:10:46.050 --> 00:10:51.050
- Not to judge no one
and never turn your eye,

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:55.160
a blind eye, when a person is in need.

00:10:55.160 --> 00:10:59.490
Or need of your advice or something.

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:01.000
I get stopped a lot.

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:03.110
And I tell people how to change their life

00:11:03.110 --> 00:11:06.340
because of my experience
I have went through.

00:11:06.340 --> 00:11:07.393
I say, you know what?

00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:09.690
They say how do you get an apartment?

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:13.090
Come on, I take them through the steps.

00:11:13.090 --> 00:11:15.600
I say you got to go
through these steps, now.

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:17.215
Now, if you ain't willing to,

00:11:17.215 --> 00:11:18.885
you ain't going to get no apartment

00:11:18.885 --> 00:11:20.470
And some of them never get an apartment

00:11:20.470 --> 00:11:23.240
but you don't want to obey His steps.

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:25.310
But I had to obey a lot of steps

00:11:25.310 --> 00:11:27.853
to have an apartment that I got now.

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:31.850
- [Mark] What's your view of
your childhood that you had?

00:11:31.850 --> 00:11:34.290
Your dad was out of
your life, your mom was,

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:35.450
- Well,
- do you regret?

00:11:35.450 --> 00:11:37.313
- First, yes, I regret.

00:11:37.313 --> 00:11:39.102
- having the parents that you did?

00:11:39.102 --> 00:11:41.502
- Yeah. Yes. I regret
everything they did to me.

00:11:42.841 --> 00:11:44.641
But I forgive them at the same time.

00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:49.530
On my mom died, on her death bed

00:11:49.530 --> 00:11:54.530
in the hospital, somebody in
the drug pool that I was in

00:11:55.470 --> 00:11:57.423
found out where my mind was and

00:11:58.430 --> 00:12:00.827
they took me over there to see my mom.

00:12:01.690 --> 00:12:04.023
I only seen her for
seven days and she died.

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:08.840
She had Alzheimer's, she don't
even know who I was anyway.

00:12:08.840 --> 00:12:12.720
But I just was able to
see her after 48 years.

00:12:12.720 --> 00:12:15.680
I see my mom when she was
young and big and healthy.

00:12:15.680 --> 00:12:19.120
Now she's frail gray hair and bawled up.

00:12:19.120 --> 00:12:21.243
No, I told them no that ain't my mama.

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:23.390
No, that ain't mama.

00:12:23.390 --> 00:12:25.530
I couldn't believe that was my mama.

00:12:25.530 --> 00:12:29.383
See 48 years, how much 48
years changes a person.

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:32.840
And sometimes when I be
telling these stories,

00:12:32.840 --> 00:12:37.350
I be crying, but I be
crying from the inside.

00:12:37.350 --> 00:12:38.850
You'd never see a teardrop,

00:12:38.850 --> 00:12:41.453
but on the inside, I've
been crying all my life.

00:12:42.380 --> 00:12:44.330
I've been crying all my life.

00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:46.600
But God's been crying with me.

00:12:46.600 --> 00:12:47.677
I've been crying all my life.

00:12:47.677 --> 00:12:50.664
And I tell everybody that.

00:12:50.664 --> 00:12:52.645
They say, you seem so happy, David.

00:12:52.645 --> 00:12:54.240
It's just, if you only knew.

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:55.123
if you only knew,

00:12:57.190 --> 00:12:58.943
If you only knew is I'm not happy.

00:13:01.312 --> 00:13:02.762
- [Mark] Do you feel like all the things

00:13:02.762 --> 00:13:04.790
you've been through have
helped make you stronger?

00:13:04.790 --> 00:13:08.010
- Yes. The abuse made me stronger.

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:09.950
The neglect made me stronger.

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:12.223
The lack of love made me stronger.

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:16.930
The kindness made me stronger.

00:13:16.930 --> 00:13:19.150
You know, everything made me stronger.

00:13:19.150 --> 00:13:22.373
God made it right for me,
everything right for me.

00:13:24.380 --> 00:13:25.760
- [Mark] What emotions do you deal with?

00:13:25.760 --> 00:13:27.810
Do you get depressed sometimes?

00:13:27.810 --> 00:13:30.860
- No, I tried not to get depressed.

00:13:30.860 --> 00:13:34.810
I go walking or something or recycling.

00:13:34.810 --> 00:13:37.980
I don't like to feel depression, no.

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:42.310
I take right now hypertension
pills for depression.

00:13:47.282 --> 00:13:48.950
- [Mark] So you you've had
depression in the past?

00:13:48.950 --> 00:13:51.650
- Yes.
- The medication helps you?

00:13:51.650 --> 00:13:52.483
- Yes.

00:13:59.774 --> 00:14:03.024
- [Mark] What was your favorite memory?

00:14:10.728 --> 00:14:13.540
- To tell you the truth, I don't have one.

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:15.993
I was trying to think of one, but I can't.

00:14:18.550 --> 00:14:22.070
No, I can't, I don't know.

00:14:31.670 --> 00:14:34.253
Oh, okay, I found out one.

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:39.173
When I went and purchased
me a little duck.

00:14:40.290 --> 00:14:43.120
So I have my little duck in my apartment

00:14:43.120 --> 00:14:44.690
it's living in the bathroom.

00:14:44.690 --> 00:14:47.313
He's poo-pooing every damn where.

00:14:48.198 --> 00:14:49.660
And I'm like oh hell now, I can't even

00:14:49.660 --> 00:14:52.057
walk in my bathroom
without stepping in it.

00:14:52.057 --> 00:14:54.450
But I raised him from little chick

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:57.350
all the way to like this, a big, big duck.

00:14:57.350 --> 00:14:59.370
So, I mean, he was like a dog.

00:14:59.370 --> 00:15:00.320
He was like a dog.

00:15:00.320 --> 00:15:02.510
I was like, come here, come here

00:15:02.510 --> 00:15:05.160
he'll look at me, I say,
come here, come here.

00:15:05.160 --> 00:15:07.020
He look he'll, he'll go.

00:15:07.020 --> 00:15:10.170
He'll come to me, he'll
stay right by my leg.

00:15:10.170 --> 00:15:13.610
And nibble on my pant,
but he'll come to me.

00:15:13.610 --> 00:15:18.320
I had it for a month, but my
therapist, my psychiatrist

00:15:18.320 --> 00:15:22.660
told me, David, let's
take them to a shelter.

00:15:22.660 --> 00:15:25.190
I said, take him to a
shelter, no, for what?

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:27.810
Cause he's getting too big, he's too big

00:15:27.810 --> 00:15:30.650
and your apartment is too
small for him to run around.

00:15:30.650 --> 00:15:32.613
He needs space.

00:15:33.816 --> 00:15:37.263
I let her talk me into
taking him to a shelter.

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:41.320
So that was one of my joyfullest times.

00:15:41.320 --> 00:15:44.647
Being able to watch him
grow and talk to him,

00:15:44.647 --> 00:15:46.253
and he respond.

00:15:48.050 --> 00:15:49.873
- [Mark] Given the life that you've had,

00:15:49.873 --> 00:15:51.913
do you feel like life is unfair?

00:15:54.530 --> 00:15:57.500
- Well, I don't know
if it's fair or unfair.

00:15:57.500 --> 00:15:58.350
I don't know.

00:15:58.350 --> 00:16:01.300
I don't know how to answer
if it's fair or unfair.

00:16:01.300 --> 00:16:03.900
I just know life is life.

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:04.900
Life is life.

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:06.063
Life is what it is.

00:16:07.700 --> 00:16:09.033
You can't change it.

00:16:10.151 --> 00:16:11.510
So why try to figure it out?

00:16:11.510 --> 00:16:16.460
Just go along with life and
you'll be better off (laughs)

00:16:18.429 --> 00:16:19.262
- [Mark] All right, David,

00:16:19.262 --> 00:16:20.095
thank you so much for sharing your story.

00:16:20.095 --> 00:16:21.700
- Oh, you welcome.

00:16:21.700 --> 00:16:24.030
Thank you man, for having me.

00:16:24.030 --> 00:16:25.280
- [Mark] Yeah. Very interesting.

00:16:25.280 --> 00:16:27.170
- Yeah.
- Thank you very much.

00:16:27.170 --> 00:16:32.030
- See, and everything I
told you is from my heart.

00:16:32.030 --> 00:16:35.950
A lot of secrets I hope I
wouldn't let certain people know

00:16:35.950 --> 00:16:40.257
but the ones who don't need
to know, they will never know.

00:16:40.257 --> 00:16:44.920
But I let you know what I'm all about.

00:16:44.920 --> 00:16:46.863
- Thank you very much.
- You're welcome.

